                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This is a fun little roguelite experience if you're into the zombie survival vibe but also love turn-based RPGs. The gameplay is a little repetitive, and honestly, I find the normal difficulty to feel just challenging enough that you feel pressured most of the time, but it's mostly manageable. It took one failed playthrough (played maybe an hour or two before deciding I should restart) to determine what would work better for a second, and I think that'll probably be true for most new players unless you look up some help. There's a small narrative, though it remains mostly a run-based game where you manage supplies and send folks out on a run every day. [i]It says it has controller support, but I've never gotten a controller to work, so I would not count on that as a feature[/i]. Not much else to say here. If you want zombie survival and you're an RPG nut, easy win here.",
